# Code Quality (Node.js)

## TypeScript

- **Strict:** strict, noUncheckedIndexedAccess, noImplicitReturns, noFallthroughCasesInSwitch
- **Config:** module NodeNext; path aliases (@/*); exclude test and build output from root tsconfig
- **Types:** Explicit function return types for public APIs; avoid any; use unknown and narrow

## Naming

- **Files:** kebab-case or PascalCase for components; consistent per project
- **Variables/functions:** camelCase; constants UPPER_SNAKE when true constants
- **Interfaces/types:** PascalCase; I-prefix optional (e.g. User or IUser)

## Structure

- **Layers:** Controllers → services → repositories (or domain); shared (clients, errors, utils); test (setup, factories)
- **Single responsibility:** One main export per file; small modules
- **Imports:** Prefer path aliases; group (external, internal, types); no circular deps

## Tooling

- **ESLint:** TypeScript and recommended rules; fix on save
- **Prettier:** Consistent formatting; run with ESLint without conflict (eslint-config-prettier)
- **Pre-commit:** Lint and format; optional type-check

## Conventions

- Strict TypeScript; consistent naming; layered structure; no dead code; fail fast on invalid config
- See patterns/clean-code.mdc for general principles

## Anti-Patterns

- any; unchecked indexed access; large files; circular dependencies; inconsistent naming

**See also:** `../../patterns/clean-code.mdc`, `testing.mdc`
